hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15482","Muawiyah ibn Hisham Abu al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Shabi, he said: Muti ibn al-Aswad said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest: No Qurashi should be killed after this day of his in captivity."
"15483","Waki narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, from Amir, from Abd Allah ibn Muti, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the day of the conquest of Makkah: No Qurashi will be killed in captivity after today until the Day of Resurrection."
"15484","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar, from Amir al-Shabi, from Abd Allah ibn Muti ibn al-Aswad, brother of Banu Adi ibn Kab, from his father Muti, and his name was al-As, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Muti. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he ordered the killing of this group in Makkah, saying: Makkah will not be raided after this year ever, and no man of Quraysh will be killed after the year in captivity ever."
"15485","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Zakariya, Amir narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muti, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah saying: No Qurashi will be killed in captivity after today. And Islam did not overtake any of the disobedient of Quraysh except Muti. And his name was Asi, so he named him Muti, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
